# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# 1. The Open Graph images.
#
#    Next's metadata route emits `fr/opengraph-image` — a real 1200x630 PNG with
#    NO file extension. Static hosts derive Content-Type from the extension, so
#    without this rule the file goes out as application/octet-stream and every
#    scraper that fetches it (WhatsApp, Facebook, iMessage, Slack, Twitter)
#    silently drops the preview image. The link still shares; it just shares
#    naked. That matters more than usual here because the site's own demo CTA
#    is a wa.me link, so WhatsApp is the channel the page is most often pasted
#    into.
#
#    Kept as three explicit paths rather than a wildcard: `/*/opengraph-image`
#    would also match any future locale, which is the intent, but Pages matches
#    a bare `*` greedily across slashes and the explicit form is unambiguous.

/fr/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/en/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/ar/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png

# 2. Next's fingerprinted bundles.
#
#    Everything under `_next/static` carries a content hash in its filename, so
#    a given URL's bytes never change. Year-long immutable caching is the
#    contract that filename is making; without it the CDN revalidates 2 MB of
#    unchanged JavaScript on every visit.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
